{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark thee noble traveler bound for Japan’s fair shores\nThy quest doth begin at Tokyo’s gates where neon doth gleam bright\nUpon thy first morn rise early and to Shibuya’s crossroads haste\nWhere multitudes do weave through streets both vibrant and wild\nDo gaze upon the giant screens that blare with voices unseen\nAnd taste the delights of ramen hot or waffles sweet that call thee near.\n\nNow journey forth unto Asakusa’s old streets where temples stand\nThe Sensō-ji’s vermillion gates shall thrill thy sight anew\nDo bow with grace and pray at the hall where incense doth rise\nThen wander through stalls where trinkets and souvenirs do gleam\nBuy a fortune slip and ponder what fate doth whisper thee\nYet fear not for Japan’s kindness shall guide thee safe and sure.\n\nAye lo the Shinkansen’s swift steed shall bear thee on thy way\nTo Kyoto’s halls where ancient whispers linger still\nThe Fushimi Inari’s torii gates do climb in endless row\nTheir crimson paths shall lead thee high unto the misty skies\nThen lose thyself within the bamboo forest’s dance and sway\nWhere time itself doth seem to pause in quiet majesty.\n\nLo at Gion’s twilight do the geisha glide with measured tread\nTheir silk and fans do paint the evening gold\nDo seek a teahouse where the master pours with gentle hand\nAnd sip the matcha’s bittersweet that calms thy wandering soul\nThen let the riverside lanterns light thy path unto the end.\n\nNow turn thy gaze unto Nara’s fields where deer do roam at will\nThey nuzzle thy palms for treats of crackers sweet and plain\nThe Todai-ji’s giant Buddha doth watch o’er thee with grace\nHis bronze eyes hold secrets older than thy kin’s own name\nDo feed the birds and listen as their cries do blend with the breeze.\n\nSwiftly then unto Osaka’s bustle where castles stand so proud\nThe Osaka Castle’s spires do pierce the heavens high above\nThen do feast upon takoyaki’s round delights so warm and crisp\nLet kushikatsu’s deep-fried splendor bathe thy tongue in joy\nAnd drink the sake that flows like laughter through the taverns deep.\n\nAye now the bullet train doth bear thee westward once more\nTo Hiroshima’s peace where shadows of the past still cling\nDo bow in silence at the park where sorrow doth abide\nThen let the Miyajima torii rise from waters calm and deep\nA red bridge that doth mirror heaven’s own embrace so pure.\n\nReturn to Kobe where steak doth reign supreme and mariners do call\nThe port’s cool breezes whisper tales of voyages long past\nThen ride the ropeway high above the harbor’s blue expanse\nWhere Arima’s hot springs shall cleanse thy bones and weary limbs\n\nLo thy final days in Hakone where mountains kiss the sea\nDo bathe in onsen’s steaming waters warm as love’s own embrace\nAnd gaze upon the Fuji’s crown when clear skies allow thee\nHer snowy peak shall crown thy journey with celestial art.\n\nThus ends thy sojourn through Japan’s fair land both old and new\nWhere ancient spirits dance with modern lights in endless play\nReturn with stories rich and treasures held both deep and bright\nFor none shall tread this path and not be changed forevermore.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -3.4242587089538574}, {"token": "e", "logprob": -0.0010324153117835522}, {"token": " noble", "logprob": -2.456023693084717}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.3287191092967987}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0002734287118073553}, {"token": " bound", "logprob": -0.706890344619751}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.009332484565675259}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -1.599003553390503}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.23700125515460968}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.06423230469226837}, {"token": " shores", "logprob": -1.0711625814437866}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.15508095920085907